","description":"\u003cp\u003eThis tag is initially being created specifically for the Directory Cards componenet on aws.amazon.com/health/case-studies/. When the GCRP decided to add multilingual content to the CSDIR in 2023, the owners of this page only wanted to display the English content in our Directory. Because the Directory Cards component on their page uses an OR operator to pull in content from two tags, they would be unable to add a prefilter condition to look for only English content. This can only be done if the page is using an AND operator. Thus, this tag will be autoapplied to all content that meets the current prefilter conditions. At that point, the page owners can use the AND operator to display content with this tag and GLOBAL#language#english.\u003c/p\u003e\n","dateCreated":"2023-04-26T20:23:44+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-04-26T20:23:44+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"customer-references#trueblue05182022sljsdgosi","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"customer-references","name":"trueblue05182022sljsdgosi","dateCreated":"2023-02-08T01:16:38+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-02-08T01:38:42+0000","additionalFields":{"descriptionSummary":"When TrueBlue wanted to accurately match blue collar jobs to North American workers, they decided they wanted to build a serverless data processing solution that not only scaled but easy to manage. In this episode Director of Data Science Engineering Carlos Lara dives into how they use the AWS Database Migration Service to extract data, and Amazon EventBridge and Amazon SQS to do time sequenced processing of it. We also explore how they use AWS Step Functions to orchestrate a workflow of Glue jobs to perform continuous upserts into table snapshots for data scientists to consume.","imageSrcUrl":"https://d1.awsstatic.com/Customer%20References%20Directory%20Logos/TrueBlue_Logo%401x.7cf92df9eb26865c375af32d14f6cf9003d26ae6.png","displayLocation":"United States","customerNameLower":"trueblue, inc.","footerInfoText":"Published Date","industry":"Professional Services","sortDate":"2022-05-18","headlineUrl":"https://youtu.be/iKYvG5aiIn8?did\u003dcr_card\u0026trk\u003dcr_card","customer-name":"Trueblue, Inc.","publishedDate":"2022","enableShare":"1","headline":"TrueBlue: Scaling Job Matching with a Serverless Delta Lake","contentType":"Customer Story"}},"tags":[{"id":"customer-references#customer-segment#enterprise","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"customer-references#customer-segment","name":"Enterprise","description":"Enterprise","dateCreated":"2019-07-22T18:39:40+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-05T01:27:39+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#product#sqs","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#product","name":"Amazon Simple Queue Service (SQS)","description":"Amazon Simple Queue Service (SQS)","dateCreated":"2020-03-02T07:05:36+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:33:02+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#tech-category#serverless","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#tech-category","name":"Serverless","description":"Serverless","dateCreated":"2021-07-28T18:46:39+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:35:33+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#product#glue","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#product","name":"AWS Glue","description":"AWS Glue","dateCreated":"2020-03-02T07:03:41+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:32:39+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#location#americas","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#location","name":"Americas","description":"Americas","dateCreated":"2020-02-03T05:29:01+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:29+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#tech-category#app-integration","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#tech-category","name":"Application Integration","description":"Application Integration","dateCreated":"2020-01-16T17:43:04+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:35:22+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#video","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Video","description":"Video","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:43+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:11+0000"},{"id":"customer-references#category#databases","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"customer-references#category","name":"Databases","description":"Databases","dateCreated":"2019-07-22T18:31:42+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-12T02:01:30+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#product#eventbridge","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#product","name":"Amazon EventBridge","description":"Amazon EventBridge","dateCreated":"2020-03-02T07:03:23+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:32:36+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#location#united-states","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#location","name":"United States","description":"United States","dateCreated":"2020-02-03T05:29:08+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:34+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#location#namer","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#location","name":"North America","description":"North America","dateCreated":"2020-02-03T05:29:03+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:34+0000"},{"id":"customer-references#category#big-data-analytics","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"customer-references#category","name":"Big Data \u0026 Analytics","description":"Big Data \u0026 Analytics","dateCreated":"2019-07-22T18:31:04+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-19T05:00:36+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#industry#prof-services","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#industry","name":"Professional Services","description":"Professional Services","dateCreated":"2020-06-25T04:07:49+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:32:08+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#product#s3","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#product","name":"Amazon Simple Storage Service (S3)","description":"Amazon Simple Storage Service (S3)","dateCreated":"2020-03-02T07:05:09+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:32:58+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#customer-story","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Customer Story","description":"Customer Story","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:24+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:07+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#product#step-functions","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#product","name":"AWS Step Functions","description":"AWS Step Functions","dateCreated":"2020-03-02T07:05:39+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:33:02+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#tech-category#databases","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#tech-category","name":"Databases","description":"Databases","dateCreated":"2020-01-16T17:43:14+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:35:27+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#tech-category#storage","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#tech-category","name":"Storage","description":"Storage","dateCreated":"2020-01-16T17:43:35+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:35:33+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#tech-category#analytics","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#tech-category","name":"Analytics","description":"Analytics","dateCreated":"2020-01-16T17:43:03+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:35:22+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#customer-segment#enterprise","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#customer-segment","name":"Enterprise (ENT)","description":"Enterprise (ENT)","dateCreated":"2021-06-04T06:35:40+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:14+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#language#english","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#language","name":"English","description":"English","dateCreated":"2020-03-03T06:40:42+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:23+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#reference-arch-diagram","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Reference Architecture Diagram","description":"Reference Architecture Diagram","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:31+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:09+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"customer-references#swimmingau05092022ljkshneflijas","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"customer-references","name":"swimmingau05092022ljkshneflijas","dateCreated":"2023-02-08T01:16:49+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-03-02T02:48:50+0000","additionalFields":{"descriptionSummary":"Having won 9 gold, 3 silver, and 8 bronze medals along with setting a new world record in the woman\u0027s 4x100 freestyle relay in Tokyo 2021, the Australian Olympic Swim team delivered their most successful Olympic games ever.\nJoin builder Gerardo Estaba on this special episode of This is My Architecture as he explores how Swimming Australia use machine learning in the AWS cloud to assist swimming coaches with their relay order decisions. We explore how historical swimming results and other swimming data are ingested in the cloud, transformed and then used to train a machine learning algorithm that\u0027s queried by coaches using a custom app to help them predict swimming times and the best possible relay order.\n\nWe dive into Swimming Australia\u0027s event-driven architecture for their relay order prediction system, to understand how they ingest, transform and orchestrate data using AWS Glue, AWS Step Functions and Amazon Simple Storage Service (S3). We also learn how they leverage Amazon Athena and Amazon SageMaker to build, train, and deploy the relay order machine learning models, and how they leverage Amazon Aurora, AWS Lambda and Amazon API Gateway to process requests from the coaches application.","imageSrcUrl":"https://d1.awsstatic.com/Customer%20References%20Directory%20Logos/swimming-australia-logo%401x.116d6fce066e744ffc6ba885a1b612087a86679b.png","displayLocation":"Asia Pacific","customerNameLower":"swimming australia","footerInfoText":"Published Date","industry":"Professional Services","sortDate":"2022-05-09","headlineUrl":"https://youtu.be/1VcpCVe3tLQ?did\u003dcr_card\u0026trk\u003dcr_card","customer-name":"Swimming Australia","publishedDate":"2022","enableShare":"1","headline":"Swimming Australia: Going For Gold With Machine Learning","contentType":"Customer Story"}},"tags":[{"id":"customer-references#customer-segment#enterprise","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"customer-references#customer-segment","name":"Enterprise","description":"Enterprise","dateCreated":"2019-07-22T18:39:40+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-05T01:27:39+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#location#apac","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#location","name":"Asia Pacific","description":"Asi